@startuml ROI Comparison
!theme plain

title TestCaptive - ROI Analysis: Manual vs TestCaptive

participant "QA Engineer" as QA
participant "TestCaptive" as TC
participant "Generated Test" as Test
participant "CI/CD Pipeline" as CICD

== Traditional Manual Approach ==

group Manual Test Creation (8-16 hours per test)
    QA -> QA: Analyze requirements (1 hr)
    QA -> QA: Design test cases (1 hr)
    QA -> QA: Write test code manually (4-8 hrs)
    note right
      - Research framework syntax
      - Find selectors manually (inspect element)
      - Write assertions
      - Handle waits/timeouts
      - Debug syntax errors
    end note
    QA -> QA: Create test data (1 hr)
    QA -> QA: Debug and fix issues (2-4 hrs)
    QA -> Test: Commit test to repository
end

group Test Maintenance (4-8 hours per UI change)
    QA -> QA: UI changed, test broke
    QA -> QA: Find broken selectors
    QA -> QA: Update code manually
    QA -> QA: Re-test and debug
end

note over QA
  **Cost per Test: $400-$800**
  (assuming $50/hr)
  
  **Annual Maintenance: $200-$400/test**
  
  **For 100 tests: $40,000-$80,000**
end note

== TestCaptive Approach ==

group TestCaptive Test Creation (1-2 hours per test)
    QA -> TC: Record user flow (15 min)
    activate TC
    TC -> TC: Smart event capture
    TC -> TC: Extract selectors automatically
    TC -> TC: Generate Playwright test code
    TC -> Test: Export ready-to-use tests
    deactivate TC
    
    QA -> Test: Review and customize (30 min)
    note right
      - Add assertions (if needed)
      - Adjust waits
      - Customize data
    end note
    QA -> CICD: Integrate with pipeline (15 min)
end

group Test Maintenance (1 hour per UI change)
    QA -> TC: Re-record affected flow (10 min)
    TC -> Test: Generate updated test (5 min)
    QA -> Test: Review changes (15 min)
    QA -> CICD: Deploy update (5 min)
end

note over QA, TC
  **Cost per Test: $50-$100**
  (assuming $50/hr)
  
  **Annual Maintenance: $50/test**
  
  **For 100 tests: $5,000-$10,000**
  
  ⭐ **80-90% Cost Reduction**
  ⭐ **10x Faster Test Creation**
  ⭐ **Enable non-technical QA**
end note

== ROI Summary ==

note over QA, CICD
  **Year 1 Savings (100 tests):**
  Manual: $40,000 - $80,000
  TestCaptive: $5,000 - $10,000
  **SAVINGS: $35,000 - $70,000**
  
  **Additional Benefits:**
  ✅ Faster time-to-market
  ✅ Better test coverage
  ✅ Reduced technical debt
  ✅ Enable business analysts to write tests
  ✅ Consistent test quality
  ✅ Playwright-powered testing
end note

@enduml
